h locally higher amounts\npossible. Winds gusting as high as 45 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Northwest San Juan Mountains and Southwest San Juan\nMountains.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult to impossible. The\nhazardous conditions will impact the Monday morning commute.","ends":"2026-11-02T12:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Weather Advisory","headline":"Winter Weather Advisory issued November 1 at 7:52PM MST until November 2 at 6:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Snow expected above 10000 feet. Total snow accumulations\nbetween 5 and 10 inches. Locally higher amounts possible. Winds\ngusting as high as 35 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Flat Tops, Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys,\nGrand and Battlement Mesas, and West Elk and Sawatch Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult.","ends":"2026-11-02T18:00:00-07:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Grand and Battlement Mesas; Gore and Elk Mountains/Central Mountain Valleys; West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Flat Tops","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.003.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b284c983150236c87728b60844c957442b4b55be.003.1"},{"event":"Avalanche Advisory","headline":"Avalanche Advisory issued October 31 at 7:16PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SABCO\n\nTHE FOLLOWING MESSAGE IS TRANSMITTED AT THE REQUEST OF THE\nCOLORADO AVALANCHE INFORMATION CENTER.\n\n...A SPECIAL AVALANCHE ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4:30 PM SATURDAY\nUNTIL 4:30 PM MONDAY...\n\n*WHAT...Avalanche conditions are dangerous above treeline.\n*WHERE...West Elk Mountains, Elk Mountains, San Juan Mountains, and\nLa Plata Mountains\n*WHEN...From 4:30 PM Saturday until 4:30 PM Monday.\n*IMPACTS...Backcountry travelers can easily trigger dangerous\navalanches large enough to bury a human.\n\n*PRECAUTION/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...A potent winter storm increases\navalanche danger Sunday into Monday. Rain, snow, and wind will cause\nnatural avalanches above treeline. Check the forecast at\nwww.colorado.gov/avalanche.\n\nBeyer & Pritchett","ends":"2026-11-02T16:30:00-07:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-02T12:19:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 021219 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 519 AM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Several rivers across SW Colorado are forecast to crest overnight Sunday into Monday. - The San Juan River at Pagosa Springs is forecast to reach major flood stage which has prompted the continuation of the Particularly Dangerous Situation Flood Warning for","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-02T06:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-021100- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1135 PM MST Sun Nov 1 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"oth01","station_name":"Olathe